# Keep local state out of the build context. Anything listed here is invisible to
# `docker build`, which matters twice: .env or storage/ leaking into the image
# would ship one environment's secrets and cache files to production, and a
# changing vendor/ or node_modules/ would bust the layer cache on every build.
#
# docker/production/ is deliberately NOT ignored: the Dockerfile copies the php
# and entrypoint files from it.

# Both forms are needed: a bare pattern matches the context root only, so
# `.env.*` alone would still copy a deploy env file written next to the compose
# file straight into the image.
.env
.env.*
**/.env
**/.env.*
!.env.example

.git
.gitignore
.github

vendor
node_modules

# Recreated with the right ownership by the Dockerfile, and carried across
# deploys by the external storage volume.
storage
bootstrap/cache

# Test and tooling artifacts.
tests
.phpunit.cache
.phpunit.result.cache
.pest
coverage
build

# Editor and OS noise.
.idea
.vscode
.fleet
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# Documentation and local compose files, none of which the image needs.
docker-compose.override.yml
*.md
!README.md
